.TH EUCLID-CLI-ETS-LIST-SERVERS 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ets-list-servers \- list the defined transfer servers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ets list-servers
[\fB\-\-prefix\fR|\fB\-x\fR \fIPREFIX\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists the defined transfer servers, ordered by server ID, each with its
protocol, address and port, the bucket it fronts, the EAM users and
groups allowed to log in, and its state.
.PP
Each entry carries two states, and the difference between them is the
point of this command:
.TP
.I desiredState
What
.BR euclid-cli-ets-start-server (1)
or
.BR euclid-cli-ets-stop-server (1)
last asked for - \fIRUNNING\fR or \fISTOPPED\fR.
.TP
.I state
What the manager currently has running, read from its own pool of
processes.
.PP
The two differ for a few seconds while a server is coming up or going
down. A server whose
.I desiredState
stays
.I RUNNING
while its
.I state
stays
.I STOPPED
is failing to start - the usual causes are a port already in use, a
missing or unreadable SSH host key, or an unwritable spool directory.
The reason is logged by the
.BR euclid-ftp (8)
or
.BR euclid-sftp (8)
process itself.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-prefix " " \fIPREFIX\fR
Only list servers whose ID starts with this prefix. Defaults to empty,
which lists every server.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The list was retrieved; the servers are printed as JSON under
\fIservers\fR. An empty list is still a success.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, the caller is not an authenticated administrator, or
the server could not be reached.
.SH EXAMPLES
List every server:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ets list-servers
.fi
.RE
.PP
List only the SFTP ones, given a naming convention:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ets list-servers \e
    --prefix sftp
.fi
.RE
.PP
Watch a server come up after starting it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ets start-server \e
    --server-id sftp1
sleep 10
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ets list-servers \e
    --prefix sftp1
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ets (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ets-get-server (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ets-start-server (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ets-stop-server (1),
.BR euclid-cli-emm-list-modules (1)
